Z||000015||Boomtastic||07-08-2001||08:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B> That picture was taken Aug. 1991 at IRP in Indianapolis. It was a Big Block brought to the show by Gary Zumwalt. Looked pretty impressive for the show but it was trailered in and we watched Gary push it off and back on the trailer. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I couldn't see the picture, but if it is the one I'm thinking of (white Fiero with white motor and tunnel ram setup), I have it on video in Carlisle PA circa 1993. (No - not running!) Most of the parts required to complete the project were made from billet T6061-T6 aluminum. I have the hand out from that show with the detailed parts descriptions - very impressive! At that time, Zumalt was selling his kit through Hertiage A & F of Posen, IL, which I believe has since gone out of business.||||reg||3
